ch mainstream, pop orientated material. Cole was one of the first African Americans to host a television variety show, with \"The Nat King Cole Show\" premiering on November 5, 1956,  on NBC.\r\n His numerous awards include the Grammy Lifetime Achievement Award in 1990, and being inducted into the Down Beat Jazz Hall of Fame in 1997 and into the Rock And Roll Hall of Fame in 2000 as a major influence on early rock & roll.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:145288","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":948466,"name":"Eddie Laguna"},{"id":1764662,"name":"Aye Guy"},{"id":2730290,"name":"\"Shorty\" Nadine"},{"id":6099913,"name":"Lord Calvert (2)"},{"id":6710830,"name":"Sam Schmaltz"},{"id":7296830,"name":"Nature Boy (14)"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":284742,"name":"The International Jazzmen"},{"active":true,"id":311056,"name":"Metronome All Stars"},{"active":true,"id":320797,"name":"The Nat King Cole Trio"},{"active":true,"id":446625,"name":"Lester Young Trio"},{"active":true,"id":446664,"name":"The Just Jazz All Stars"},{"active":true,"id":875290,"name":"Eddie Cole's Solid Swingers"},{"active":true,"id":2261700,"name":"Lester Young-Buddy Rich Trio"},{"active":true,"id":3678154,"name":"Metronome All-Star Band"},{"active":true,"id":3800795,"name":"King Cole Quartet"},{"active":true,"id":5460167,"name":"The Keynoters (3)"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["\"King Cole\"","\"King\" Cole","\"Nat\" King Cole","'King' Cole","A. Cole","Aye Guy Alias Nat King Cole","Chloe","Cle","Cole","Cole Nat King","Cole, Nat King","Coles","K. Cole","King","King Cole","Kole","N .K. Cole","N King Cole","N. \"King\" Cole","N. ''King'' Cole","N. Cole","N. K. Cole","N. King Cole","N.Cole","N.K. Cole","N.K.Cole","N.King Cole","NK Cole","Nast","Nast King Cole","Nat","Nat  Cole","Nat \"KIng\" Cole","Nat \"King\" Cole","Nat \"King\" Cole With Orch.","Nat \"King\" Cole With Orchestra","Nat \"King\" Cole,","Nat \"King” Cole","Nat \"King„ Cole","Nat \"Ring\" Coles","Nat ''King\" Cole","Nat ''King'